# Settings form section (title + description + Card)

Use for stacked settings blocks that mirror **Settings → Appearance** (`/settings/appearance`): a **tight** stack of **title** (`h2`) + **description** (`p`), then a clear gap, then controls inside **`SettingsFormCard`** (via `SettingsFormSection`).

## Rules

- **Do not** put `h2`, description `p`, and `Card` as **direct siblings** under `space-y-2` — that adds extra gap between title and description (Tailwind spaces every child).
- **Do** wrap **title + description** (+ optional **note**) in a **single** `<div>` so only **one** `space-y-2` step sits between that intro block and the card.
- Prefer **`SettingsFormSection`** from `@engenty/ui-core` instead of hand-rolling the markup.

## Component

- **`SettingsFormSection`** (`packages/ui-core/src/components/admin/settings/settings-form-section.tsx`) — wraps children in **`SettingsFormCard`**.
- **`SettingsFormCard`** (`packages/ui-core/src/components/admin/settings/settings-form-card.tsx`) — bordered settings surface; **`variant="default"`** (`p-3 sm:p-4`) or **`variant="compact"`** (`py-2` + horizontal padding for row stacks).
- Props on the section: `title`, `description`, optional `note` (smaller muted line under description), optional `cardVariant` (`compact` for {@link SettingsFormRow} stacks), `children` (rendered inside the card with default `space-y-3`; override via `cardClassName`).

## Example

```tsx
import { SettingsFormSection } from "@engenty/ui-core";

<SettingsFormSection
  title={t("sections.general")}
  description={t("sections.generalDesc")}
  note={optionalCallout}
>
  {/* rows, selects, etc. */}
</SettingsFormSection>
```

## Inside the form `Card` (no cascading cards — one surface only)

`SettingsFormSection` already wraps `children` in **`SettingsFormCard`** (border, radius, canvas panel). Use **`cardVariant="compact"`** with **`cardClassName="space-y-0 divide-y divide-border"`** when stacking {@link SettingsFormRow}s; otherwise default padding applies.

- **Do not** nest another **`Card`**, **`Card variant="default"`**, or any second **bordered + padded** panel inside `children`. That produces **double borders**, **double padding**, and the “card in a card” look that keeps regressing in reviews.
- **Tables:** render `<Table>` (and headers/rows) **directly** as `children`. Do **not** wrap the table in `<Card>…</Card>` — the table sits on the form card; `Table` supplies its own horizontal scroll wrapper when needed.
- **Subgroups:** use **dividers** (`divide-y divide-border`), **flat** tinted blocks (`rounded-md bg-muted/25 px-3 py-2`), or **spacing + typography** — not a second card chrome.

### Anti-pattern (avoid)

```tsx
<SettingsFormSection title="…" description="…">
  <Card>   {/* ❌ redundant — outer section is already a form Card */}
    <Table>...</Table>
  </Card>
</SettingsFormSection>
```

### Correct

```tsx
<SettingsFormSection title="…" description="…">
  <Table>...</Table>
</SettingsFormSection>
```

## When not to use

- List/catalog sections where the body is **not** a single form card (e.g. repeated rows only) — keep a local layout; this rule targets **headline + helper text + one form surface**.
